<section class="content">
    <div class="facts-box">
       <h3>Interesting Bear Facts</h3>

<ul>
    <li>Bears have an extremely strong sense of smell, which is much better than that of humans and even dogs.</li>
    <li>They can run faster than humans, reaching speeds of up to 40–50 km/h over short distances.</li>
    <li>Some bears, especially black bears, are excellent tree climbers.</li>
    <li>Bears have thick fur and a layer of fat that helps them survive in cold climates.</li>
    <li>They are highly intelligent animals and can remember food locations for long periods.</li>
    <li>Many bears are solitary animals and prefer to live alone except during mating season.</li>
    <li>Bears communicate using sounds, body language, and scent markings.</li>
</ul>

<h3>How Bears Prepare for Winter</h3>

<ol>
    <li>They eat large amounts of food during late summer and autumn to build up fat reserves.</li>
    <li>Their bodies store this fat, which becomes their main energy source during winter.</li>
    <li>Bears find or create a den where they will stay safe during hibernation.</li>
    <li>During hibernation, their heart rate and metabolism slow down significantly.</li>
    <li>They survive for months without eating, drinking, or going to the bathroom.</li>
    <li>In spring, they wake up and begin searching for food again.</li>
</ol>
